Subject: [PATCH] KVM: riscv: keep VSTIMECMP software state in sync

kvm_riscv_vcpu_sync_interrupts() samples the hardware VSTIMECMP before
handling an SBI set_timer exit. The SSTC update path then writes only the
new hardware compare value, leaving timer.next_cycles at the old value.
If the vCPU is scheduled out before guest re-entry, timer_save() disables
the hardware comparator and timer_restore() later restores the stale
software value, overwriting the guest's new deadline and potentially
leaving a WFI vCPU asleep forever.

Update next_cycles before programming VSTIMECMP, matching the existing
hrtimer update path and preserving the new deadline across vCPU put/load.

Assisted-by: Qoder
---
 arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_timer.c
@@ -72,6 +72,9 @@
 
 static int kvm_riscv_vcpu_update_vstimecmp(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, u64 ncycles)
 {
+	struct kvm_vcpu_timer *t = &vcpu->arch.timer;
+
+	t->next_cycles = ncycles;
 #if defined(CONFIG_32BIT)
 	ncsr_write(CSR_VSTIMECMP,  ULONG_MAX);
 	ncsr_write(CSR_VSTIMECMPH, ncycles >> 32);
-- 
2.51.2
